2:/// configuration at container start as environment variables
3:/// (`FA_PROVIDER_TYPE`, `FA_PROVIDER_NAME`, plus `FA_PROVIDER_CONFIG` — or
4:/// its `FA_PROVIDER_CONFIG_BASE64` twin) plus the key itself in the env
5:/// var the config references (or that var's `_BASE64` twin), and the
6:/// harness boots that provider with no saved config. The declaration is
7:/// machine-written and self-contained: what it declares is what is used —
8:/// no catalog-guessed defaults, no env-name probing.
9:///
10:/// Precedence (wired by the host): an explicit `--provider` flag wins,
11:/// then this preconfig, then the saved config restore, then the catalog
12:/// env auto-pick, then the default. Env values arrive via an injected
13:/// reader function so this module stays pure Dart (no `dart:io`) and is
14:/// directly unit-testable.
