19:/// The [AgentService] chat surface served by the extension's service-worker
20:/// agent over a [WorkerRelayTransport] (issue #34 item 1).
21:///
22:/// The panel UI keeps its `AgentService` type — everything below the
23:/// interface seam is relayed instead of local: `sendText` becomes a
24:/// protocol `prompt` (a `steer` mid-run), the SW's host events
25:/// (`delta`/`message_done`/`tool_result`/`status`/`error`) rebuild the
26:/// transcript, and `approval_request` renders through the same approval
27:/// sheet the local path uses. The UI holds no keys and makes zero provider
28:/// fetches — the SW owns providers, tools (browser + fs), and the session.
29:///
