6:/// A [HostExtension] is a named registrant's contribution: the tools it
7:/// contributes plus an explicit state for every profile the host can
8:/// wire. The builder (lib/src/hosts/host_agent_wiring.dart) enforces the
9:/// three extension invariants:
10:///
11:/// - **E6 — declared at birth**: every built-in profile MUST have an
12:///   explicit state (`on` / `off(reason)`); there is no implicit default.
13:///   A state for a custom profile is optional at construction but
14:///   required at wire time for any profile the host actually wires.
15:/// - **E7 — collisions rejected at build time**: an extension tool id
16:///   colliding with the SDK core, the gated task surface, or another
17:///   extension throws [HostWiringException] naming both registrants. (A
18:///   tool id colliding with a CORE tool would silently override SDK
19:///   behavior — the one thing this API must never do — so the loud check
20:///   lives in the builder, not the replace-and-note [ToolRegistry], whose
21:///   leniency is the child-pool contract, issue #862.)
22:/// - **E8 — off means hidden with a reason**: on a profile whose state is
23:///   `off`, the extension's tools never reach the registry and the off
24:///   reason surfaces through [WiredAgentCore.extensions] for the host's
25:///   UI — the hide-if-off invariant, extension edition.
26:///
27:/// **Additive-only (AC9/UT-5):** the type carries tools and declarations,
28:/// nothing else — there is no member that could override a core behavior
29:/// (memory, context management, compaction, the JSONL tool session,
30:/// trajectory are SDK invariants). The only route to "replace" a core
31:/// tool is a colliding id, and E7 rejects it at build time.
32:///
33:/// Slice 6 (IT-5) pins the runtime half of that contract end-to-end:
34:/// `test/hosts/extension_host_parity_test.dart` drives the YoClip
35:/// scenario — a custom-profile host registering `yoclip.*` tools — and
36:/// asserts record-level byte parity with the CLI host (same JSONL record
37:/// kinds/payloads, same compaction trigger, same memory semantics) on the
38:/// same scripted session.
39:///
40:/// Pure Dart: no `dart:io`.
